# podssh: the generic part of its manual. The model of blocks that a
# program fills from its tables (model.rs), the man(7) writer that groff
# and mandoc render with no warning (roff.rs), the text writer (text.rs),
# the JSON of the kind of a flag (json.rs), the reader of the variables of
# the source (facts/tests.rs), the pager (pager.rs), the form of a flag row
# (flags.rs: FlagRow and FlagKind) and the check of a page under groff and
# mandoc (scripts/interop-man.sh). The facts, the notes, the examples and
# the topics of podssh stay in podssh; data.rs gives the form of the exit
# codes with the code of the remote command (facts.rs, Code::Payload).
# Of data.rs and flags.rs only the form is frozen (Code, FlagKind and
# FlagRow): a change of podssh's own text in their tables is no port.
# Imported at cfc3ae3, moved to 5340fbb (podssh's text fixes of data.rs and
# flags.rs, PodUtils/podssh@T-790). The block moved to d8e54f0, the parent
# of podssh's take of the writers (T-969): up to it each change of the block
# is podssh's own text (data.rs, flags.rs, model.rs), its own modules
# (mod.rs) or the first steps of its take (4d8c551: the model in its tests;
# ee6b6bd: --roff by the crate's writer). No change is a fix to port.
